# Third-party components and external model assets

No source code from Whisper-Streaming, WhisperLive, Voxtype, SimulStreaming, or WhisperLiveKit is copied into VoicePrompt. Word-agreement/scheduler logic is authored for this project; it does not embed an upstream HypothesisBuffer file. The community plugin directory contains no Python runtime, model weights, venv, CUDA libraries or ONNX graph.

Separately installed helper runtime dependencies are resolved in `helper/uv.lock`; their own distributions carry their licenses. Current tested packages include:

- `faster-whisper` 1.2.1, MIT, https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper . The pinned wheel includes `faster_whisper/assets/silero_vad_v6.onnx`; the helper loads that installed asset rather than copying/redistributing it into this project.
- `CTranslate2` 4.8.2, MIT, https://github.com/OpenNMT/CTranslate2 . CPU int8 supported compute types were verified on one host.
- `ONNX Runtime` 1.30.0, MIT, https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime . The Silero graph runs through its CPUExecutionProvider.
- `Silero VAD` model source, Silero Team, MIT, https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad . This product does not bundle a separate copy; the installed faster-whisper asset supplies it. Permission text and copyright are in the upstream MIT license; verify the packaged wheel license at redistribution time.
- Optional user-downloaded CPU model: `Systran/faster-whisper-small`, Hugging Face model card MIT. The model was explicitly fetched into ignored `.validation/models/cpu-small` on one test host, not distributed with the plugin/helper.
- Optional unverified CUDA model candidate: `dropbox-dash/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo`, Hugging Face model card MIT. No CUDA weights were downloaded or profiled here.

No real-user audio or user credentials are part of distributed assets. Review transitive installed package/wheel licenses before public redistribution; installing dependencies independently retains their wheel-level notices.
